                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 46-year-old male, admitted on 09/07/2002 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically suspicious for appendicitis. Diagnostic workup including laboratory analysis revealed elevated inflammatory markers (CRP, leukocytosis), and abdominal ultrasound confirmed acute appendicitis without perforation. The patient underwent uncomplicated laparoscopic appendectomy on 10/07/2002. Histopathological examination confirmed acute appendicitis. Postoperative recovery was uneventful. The patient was mobilised early, tolerated oral intake well, and received perioperative antibiotic prophylaxis. He was discharged home on 12/07/2002 in good general condition. Please arrange wound follow-up in approximately 7-10 days. Should any concerns arise, do not hesitate to contact our surgical department. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician], Department of General Surgery</div>
               </text>
